            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Jonathan M. Freiman, petitioners contend that the 1976 ex\u2011propriation exception was created because Communist states were expropriating property from U.S. nationals without compensation."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Jonathan M. Freiman",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "357e8872f65915e423556e02f675c84a38c2c15b9e0161dc88551ae29fb3686b",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-357e8872f659-0000-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioners argue that Congress has not yet taken the risk of allowing Holocaust\u2011era claims, but it could if it chose to."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Respondents",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "357e8872f65915e423556e02f675c84a38c2c15b9e0161dc88551ae29fb3686b",
